    tcp_read_line_unbounded_network_callers_2026-11-03, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep7: verified at HEAD - the migration landed via e7ee6d7af2b (4 named servers) + 4bc8ca22cac (remaining 6 ui.* sites + allowlist retirement); read_line() itself unchanged (local-file/stdio exemption per the doc). Probe: legacy read_line returns a 20001-byte unterminated line (unbounded growth tracks peer input); read_line_bounded(8192) fails closed after <=8193 bytes with the trailer intact on the socket. Guard: check-no-unbounded-tcp-read-line.shs PASS 27 files 0 unallowlisted. Spec network_server_bounded_line extended +83 lines (exactly-max_bytes incl newline -> Ok; max_bytes+1 -> Err with trailer intact) 3/3 PASS; neighbours cli_socket 11/11, count_guard 1/1, content_length guards, async_web 28/28, tcp_socket_resource_wrapper 7/7. Residuals (named scope exclusions, recorded): proxy.spl upstream status/header lines bounded only after one buffered line; play/cdp/client handshake lines capped by iteration count only; the gc_async_mut async wrappers expose read_line without a bounded variant (guard cannot see async callers without the literal); guard runtime ~146s on Windows Git Bash. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/app/network_server_bounded_line_spec.spl prevention=src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/io/tcp.spl"
